A comprehensive MDR service to support the protection of its users, information, systems and technology environment against cyber security threats. 
A managed cyber security service providing 24 hours a day, 7 days a week monitoring, detection, investigation and response capability, supported by appropriate security expertise, processes and technologies. 
The anticipated scope includes: 
24/7 Security Operations Centre (SOC) monitoring and response; 
Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) and/or Extended Detection and Response (XDR); 
Integration with and monitoring of Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Entra ID; 
Identity-based threat detection; 
Security alert investigation, triage and prioritisation; 
Proactive threat hunting; 
Threat intelligence; 
Incident containment and remediation support; 
Incident escalation and notification; 
Digital forensics and incident investigation; 
Integration with CHS's existing security and technology environment; 
Onboarding and deployment; 
Security reporting and service reviews; 
Vulnerability and exposure insights; 
Access to security specialists and escalation resources; 
Support during significant cyber security incidents; and 
Continual service improvement. 
Details of the following would also be beneficial: 
MDR service and operating models, including the division of responsibilities between CHS and the provider. 
Technologies deployed or integrated with in delivering MDR services. 
Integration with Microsoft 365, Microsoft Entra ID and other relevant security technologies. 
Threat detection, investigation, proactive threat hunting, containment and remediation capabilities. 
Incident response arrangements, including support for serious or high-impact cyber incidents. 
24/7 SOC operating models and SOC locations. 
Relevant security standards, certifications and independent assurance. 
Security data processing, retention, protection and residency arrangements. 
Typical severity classifications, response times and service levels. 
Reporting, customer dashboards, service reviews and security metrics. 
Onboarding, implementation and transition arrangements. 
Typical licensing and commercial models.

Jigsaw Homes Group has three operational areas which are as follows;
•	Jigsaw Homes North (Lancashire/Merseyside/Cheshire/Greater M/cr)
•	Jigsaw Homes Midlands (East Midlands)
•	Jigsaw Homes Tameside (Greater Manchester)
	The service provider shall be required to have the skills, knowledge, experience and qualifications necessary to deliver an effective programme of Window Cleaning, report on the findings and recommend all appropriate actions and produce a completion certificate to properties owned and managed by Jigsaw Homes Group (JHG) including;  
•	communal (& public) areas to residential properties;
•	JHG owned commercial properties;
•	new build properties (from developer handover onwards);
•	Any other buildings for which JHG have a responsibility for.
This service is currently managed by a couple of contractors throughout the North, Tameside & Midlands regions. It is our intention to outsource the whole of the Asset Management Communal Window Cleaning Service and split it into three Lots. The first, Lot 1 – North which covers parts of Greater Manchester, Lancashire, Cheshire & Merseyside, the second, Lot 2 – Tameside area and the third, Lot 3 – Midlands. Bidders can apply for one Lot, two or all three Lots.
The initial contract for 2 years with an option of an additional two year to a total of four years and consists of the following number per Lot;
•	Lot 1 – North 
•	Lot 2 – Tameside
•	Lot 3 - Midlands
JHG intends to enter into a Contract, please refer to Section 8 – Terms of Agreement for further details.
The successful Contractor(s) will be expected to mobilise to our timescale and be operational by 1st April 2027, please refer to Section 1.10 the Tender Process Summary below for more details.
The initial contract period runs until 31st March 2029 and if successful an extension of a year based on performance and by mutual agreement.
